The second move is equally sharp. Once the lecture has established capacity, it asks whether capacity ever becomes motion. Nico’s answer is that preparation by itself is inert: $\begin{aligned}
\mathrm{Preparation}\land \neg \mathrm{Courage}
&\Rightarrow
\mathrm{No\ decisive\ action},\\
\mathrm{Preparation}\land \mathrm{Courage}
&\Rightarrow
\mathrm{Action}\to \mathrm{Confidence}.\end{aligned}$

